Done. Both changes are implemented, build clean, and all existing tests pass.

**`rust/src/lib.rs`** — added `filter_by_tag`:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes.iter().filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag)).collect()
}
```
Exact match via `==` (not substring), preserves relative order, returns borrowed `&'a Note` (matches the existing `ordered_pinned_first` return type).

**`rust/src/main.rs`** — `list` now accepts `--tag <TAG>`. It scans the remaining args for the flag, validates that an argument is present (errors with exit 1 otherwise), and routes through `filter_by_tag` when given; otherwise lists all notes.

